*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Repo-wide normalization (2026-09-01): every text file in this repo should
# use Linux-style LF line endings, never Windows-style CRLF -- this project's
# canonical build/runtime environment is Linux (Armbian chroot, bash scripts,
# board itself), and several past bugs this session were directly caused by
# mismatched CRLF/LF assumptions (e.g. the WiFi password's D-suffix bug, and
# firstboot.conf/companion-stack.env sourcing issues). `text=auto` normalizes
# every file git detects as text to LF in the repository, regardless of what
# line endings a given checkout/editor produces locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuine binaries -- must NOT be text-normalized (would corrupt them).
*.bin binary
*.img binary
*.dtb binary
*.deb binary
*.tar binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.tar.xz binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.bmp binary
*.mp4 binary
*.so binary
*.pyc binary
